Yes, but the reason for the term "revitalizing" (which I chose, while
participating in the back-channel discussions that I think influenced the
start of this thread) is, if the LLG isn't seen as doing anything
productive, that's a failure that can be remedied by the people who wish it
would participating and then promoting action they see as serving the needs
of the Lojban community.

If you think the LLG gets nothing done, and you think this is a problem
rather than finding the organization to be irrelevant, then you can choose
to be part of the solution. There's a perception by many current Lojban
users that the LLG has failed; my response has been and will be to
encourage those who feel that way to help it succeed again.
